# Shops that may not be browsed without an account.
#
# One shop key per line. A shop listed here is built with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_REQUIRE_ACCOUNT=1, so its middleware bounces every address to the
# login except the sign-in pages and the policies named beside it.
#
# The client's requirement, in his words:
#
#   "No URL should be able to be seen without first login in. If a user sends a
#    URL to a friend, they should not be allowed to see it until they have an
#    account. The URLs with the bypass exception are: terms-of-service,
#    privacy-policy, returns-policy, shipping-policy. These pages are needed
#    when a new business signs up for an account."
#
# This lives here rather than in .estate because it is a policy about a shop,
# not a fact about where the shop is hosted, and because .estate is gitignored:
# a gate that is only recorded on one laptop is a gate that comes off the next
# time someone else builds the shop.
#
# Format: <shop> [comma-separated public paths]
# The paths default to the four policies above when the second field is absent.

b2b
